      "page_title": "Production and Orchestration",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Logging Done Right",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Write to stdout/stderr, not files inside the container",
            "Pick a log driver: json-file with rotation, or fluentd/gelf",
            "Ship logs centrally; set `max-size` and `max-file`",
            "Unbounded json-file logs ==fill disks=="
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker run -d --name api \\",
            "  --log-driver json-file \\",
            "  --log-opt max-size=10m \\",
            "  --log-opt max-file=3 \\",
            "  --memory 512m --cpus 1 \\",
            "  app@sha256:<digest>"
          ],
          "note": "no max-size means unbounded logs"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Rolling Update Flow",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Start new instance",
              "Healthcheck passes",
              "Route traffic",
              "Stop old instance",
              {
                "text": "Rollback",
                "sub": "if health fails",
                "ink": "red"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Why orchestrate at all?",
            "Swarm vs Kubernetes?",
            "How do you do zero-downtime deploys?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Production Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Ignoring SIGTERM, so connections drop at deploy",
            "Grace period shorter than your app's drain time",
            "Deploying a moving tag instead of a pinned digest",
            "Keeping state in the container, not volumes or managed DBs"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "8. Pick an Orchestrator",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Best for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Docker/Compose",
              "one host, simple"
            ],
            [
              "Swarm",
              "small clusters"
            ],
            [
              "Kubernetes",
              "large scale, rich ecosystem"
            ],
            [
              "ECS, Cloud Run",
              "managed, less ops"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 2,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "9. Health and Limits",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Healthchecks drive ==restarts== and traffic routing",
            "Route traffic only to __healthy__ instances",
            "Set memory and CPU limits on every container",
            "One service must not starve its neighbors"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "docker service create \\",
            "  --name api --replicas 3 \\",
            "  --update-delay 10s \\",
            "  --stop-grace-period 30s \\",
            "  app@sha256:<digest>"
          ],
          "note": "update-delay staggers the rollout"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "10. Graceful Shutdown",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Drain before you die",
          "text": "Handle SIGTERM, drain connections, then exit. Match the stop grace period to your app's drain time."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Key Takeaways",
          "text": "Orchestrate for healing and rollouts; keep containers stateless, limited, pinned and SIGTERM-aware."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "docker",
      "subtitle": "Run Docker at scale"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Interview Questions and Best Practices",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Core Questions, Short Answers",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Question",
            "Strong answer"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Container vs VM?",
              "Shared host kernel + namespaces/cgroups; VM = hardware + guest OS"
            ],
            [
              "Image vs container?",
              "Immutable template vs running instance + writable layer"
            ],
            [
              "COPY vs ADD?",
              "Prefer `COPY`; ADD extracts and fetches URLs"
            ],
            [
              "CMD vs ENTRYPOINT?",
              "ENTRYPOINT fixed command; CMD default args"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Size, Data and Networking",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do you reduce image size?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "==Multi-stage builds== plus slim or distroless bases",
            "Add a `.dockerignore` for the build context",
            "Clean up in the __same__ RUN layer"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "RUN apt-get update \\",
            "  && apt-get install -y curl \\",
            "  && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do containers persist data?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Named volumes, bind mounts or external storage",
            "**Never** the writable layer: it dies with the container"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do containers talk to each other?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Join one ==user-defined network==",
            "Reach peers by container or service name via DNS"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "docker network create appnet",
            "docker run -d --network appnet \\",
            "  --name db postgres:16",
            "# app dials db:5432"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Design Best Practices",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "{icon:docker} ==One process== per container",
            "==Stateless== design: state lives in volumes or services",
            "Configuration through ==environment variables==",
            "Keep images small and builds ==reproducible=="
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Ship-Safe Checklist",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Pin versions and ==digests==, never floating tags",
            "Scan images for known CVEs before pushing",
            "Run as ==non-root== with `USER`",
            "Add a `HEALTHCHECK` so orchestrators can judge health"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Build Once, Promote",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Commit",
                "sub": "git SHA"
              },
              {
                "text": "CI build",
                "sub": "image:sha"
              },
              {
                "text": "Scan + test",
                "sub": "same image"
              },
              {
                "text": "Promote",
                "sub": "stage → prod"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "CI builds ==once== and promotes the same digest; rebuilding per environment ships untested bytes.",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Common Mistakes Recap",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`:latest` tags: deploys are not reproducible",
            "Secrets baked into layers stay in history",
            "Running as root widens a breakout",
            "No log rotation fills the host disk",
            "Missing `.dockerignore` bloats and busts cache"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. Interview Point",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Interview Point",
          "items": [
            "Walk through what happens on `docker run`.",
            "How would you harden and ship a production image?",
            "How do you debug a failing container?"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
